  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added generated FLINT resource formatters for sealed ZZ and QQ polynomials, normalized their sentinel-variable pretty output to Sage display syntax, and retained the existing dynamic formatter as the portable fallback. Exact QQ coefficient materialization now uses the checked bulk reduced-rational decoder instead of constructing one host object per loop iteration. Focused tests cover repr/str equivalence, variable names, zero/unit/sign/fraction cases, skew large coefficients, forbidden coefficient materialization, portable fallback, and 20,000 rational coefficients. Representative warm degree-50k formatting measured 126.6 ms over ZZ and 166.2 ms over QQ for roughly 0.9-1.0 MB outputs. Root integration rebuilt the FLINT adapter and compiler caches and regenerated the deterministic declaration, native-boundary, test-manifest, and reference outputs.",
    "risks": [
      "The FLINT resource formatter is intentionally unavailable to Wasm; portable hosts retain the tested coefficient-based dynamic formatter."
    ],
    "next_steps": []
  }
